      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One thing I'm seeing in the telemetry is some really inconsistent temperature spikes in the semi-metallic kits during the transition phase. It's almost like the heat isn't distributing evenly, or there's some kind of unpredictable interference happening during the friction cycle. Any idea why the thermal profile would look so erratic or \"mischievous\" in the data?",
